substrate
=========

substrate turns a build output directory into a signed .zex package, and
checks, inspects and unpacks such packages. It is the package builder of
Zainium OS, by Zainium Dynamics.

  - Every pack run signs the package with a fresh Ed25519 key pair and
    keeps only the public half in it, so there is no long-lived signing key
    to leak.
  - Every package carries a BLAKE3 hash over its payload, taken in a fixed
    order, and the fs-verity digest of each file.
  - Every build runs a security pass (layout policy, hard-coded secrets)
    that stops the build when it fails.


Install
-------

  cargo install substrate-zainium

The program is called substrate.


Use
---

  substrate pack -v 2.0.0 ./my-package -o my-package-2.0.0.zex
  substrate verify  my-package-2.0.0.zex          check the signature
  substrate unpack  my-package-2.0.0.zex -o out   extract the payload
  substrate inspect my-package-2.0.0.zex          show the manifest

./my-package holds a manifest.toml (the package's metadata) and a payload/
directory (the files to install).


Format
------

  package-2.0.0.zex      zexc-compressed tar (magic ZEX1)
  ├── manifest.toml      metadata, install map, BLAKE3 hash and signature
  ├── signature.b3       BLAKE3 of the manifest and the payload hash
  └── payload/           the files, laid out as the install map says

Symlinks in payload/ stay symlinks; the hash covers their target.


